      "heading": "A - Exam authority, Safe Driving Tips",
      "learner_facing": true,
      "markdown": "## A - Exam authority, Safe Driving Tips\n\nThis dossier supports first-time never-licensed applicants preparing for the regular passenger-car written knowledge test in Kentucky. The issuing authority is the Kentucky State Police, Driver Testing Branch, and licensing services run through the Transportation Cabinet. Handbook facts in this section come from Section Eight of the Kentucky Driver Manual, covering visual search, speed and space management, stopping distance, backing, and communicating. The official question count, passing score, test format, and time limit are not stated on the assigned pages, so this dossier asserts no value for any of them. Practice scoring follows only the accepted LearningLoop product policy.\n",
